# Allow list: senders that are never screened, whatever the model says.
# Copy to allow.txt (gitignored). Generate a starting point from your own
# mailbox with `python3 src/lists.py seed` (writes to spike/proposed/).
#
# One pattern per line, case-insensitive; `#` starts a note.
#   bob@acme.com          exact address
#   @acme.com             acme.com and every subdomain (mail.acme.com)
#   *@acme.com            glob on the full address -- only acme.com itself
#   billing-*@acme.com    glob; * and ? anywhere in the address
#   name:*Acme Billing*   glob on the display name
#   re:@acme\.(com|net)$  regular expression searched in the address
#
# The most specific matching entry wins across allow and block
# (exact > glob > domain, deeper domain first > name: > re:); an exact tie
# goes to allow. Allow entries only count for authenticated mail, so a
# forged From: cannot use them.

@example.com                  # your own company
@bigcustomer.com              # you emailed them; 1200 archived
jane.doe@gmail.com            # free-mail: always per person, never @gmail.com
